# Agent workflow

Work on one deliverable at a time. Do not scaffold the entire framework in one change.

Before multi-file edits: state the approach, impacted files, and architectural effect. Implement the smallest clean change. Search the repo before creating helpers.

Never assume application features that are not in the assignment, the live app, or user instructions. State assumptions.

Do not hide Playwright failures or use empty `catch`. Preserve error cause and add a useful message.

After meaningful code changes: run typecheck and the smallest relevant Playwright scope. Do not weaken tests to force a pass.

If a user request conflicts with these rules, stop and explain the conflict. Do not silently ignore rules.
